{
  "title": "12: Yusuf يوسف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓرٰ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْن‏(1)\nALAARAA TILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE AL-MUBEEN.\nAlif, Lam, Ra. (A. L. R.); These are the verses of the Book (which makes the truth) manifest.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ قُرْءٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(2)\nINNAA ANZALNAAHO QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nVerily We have sent it down, the Arabic Qur’an that ye may understand.\nنَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ اَحْسَنَ الْقَصَصِ بِمَاۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ ۖ وَاِنْ كُنْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ لَمِنَ الْغٰفِلِيْنَ‏(3)\nNAHNO NAQUSSU A’LAYKA AHSANAL AL-QASASE BEMAA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA HAAZAA QURAANA WA KUNTA MIN QABLEHI LAMENAS AL-GHAAFELEENA.\nWe narrate unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) the most excellent of the narratives by (means of) what We have revealed unto thee this Qur’an; though thou wert before this of the unaware ones.\nاِذْ قَالَ يُوْسُفُ لِاَبِيْهِ يٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْ رَاَيْتُ اَحَدَ عَشَرَ كَوْكَبًا وَّالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ رَاَيْتُهُمْ لِىْ سٰجِدِيْنَ‏(4)\nIZ QAALA YOOSUFU LEAABEEHE YAA INNEE RAAYTU AAHADA A’ASHARA KAWKABAN WWAALSSHAMSA WAL QAMARA RAAYTUHUM LEE SAAJEDEENA.\nWhen said Joseph unto his father (Jacob): “O’ my father! Verily I did see (dreamt) eleven stars and the sun and moon, I saw them (all) prostrating unto me.\nقَالَ يٰبُنَىَّ لَا تَقْصُصْ رُءْيَاكَ عَلٰٓى اِخْوَتِكَ فَيَكِيْدُوْا لَكَ كَيْدًا ؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(5)\nQAALA YAABUNAA LAA TAQSUS RUYAAKA A’LAA AEKHWATEKA FAYAKEEDOOA LAKA KAYDAANW INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA INSAANIK A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nSaid he (Jacob): “O’ my (dear) son! (Beware!) Relate thou not thy dream unto thy brothers, lest they plot against thee a plot; Verily Satan unto man is an open enemy!\nوَكَذٰلِكَ يَجْتَبِيْكَ رَبُّكَ وَيُعَلِّمُكَ مِنْ تَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحَادِيْثِ وَيُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهٗ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰٓى اٰلِ يَعْقُوْبَ كَمَاۤ اَتَمَّهَا عَلٰٓى اَبَوَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْحٰقَ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(6)\nWA KAZAALEKA YAJTABEEKA RABBOKA WAYUA’ALLEMUKA MIN TAAWEELE AL-AAHAADEESE WAYUTEMMU NE’MATAHU A’LAYKA WA A’LAA AALE YA’QOOBAL KAMAA AATAMMAHAA A’LAA AABAWAYKA MIN QABLO IBRAAHEEMA WA ISHAAQA INNAL RABBAKA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd thus will thy Lord choose thee and teach thee the interpretation of sayings (dreams), and perfect His grace unto thee and unto the children of Jacob, even as He perfected it to thy (fore) fathers aforetime, Abraham, Isaac; Verily thy Lord is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nلَقَدْ كَانَ فِىْ يُوْسُفَ وَاِخْوَتِهٖۤ اٰيٰتٌ لِّلسَّآئِلِيْنَ‏(7)\nLAQAD KAANA FEE YOOSUFA WAAKHWATEH AAYAATUM LLELSSAAELEENA.\nIndeed there are in (the accounts of) Joseph and their brothers, signs for the inquirers.\nاِذْ قَالُوْا لَيُوْسُفُ وَاَخُوْهُ اَحَبُّ اِلٰٓى اَبِيْنَا مِنَّا وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ  ؕ اِنَّ اَبَانَا لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنِ ۖ ۚ‏(8)\nIZ QAALOO LAYOOSUFU WAAKHOOHU AAHABBU ELAA AABEENAA MINNAA WA NAHNO U’USBATUN INNAL AABAANAA LAFEE ZALAALIM MMUBEENE.\nWhen said they: “Surely Joseph and his (own) brother are dearer to our father than we, though we are (in) a (bigger) group; Verily our father is in manifest error.\nاۨقْتُلُوْا يُوْسُفَ اَوِ اطْرَحُوْهُ اَرْضًا يَّخْلُ لَكُمْ وَجْهُ اَبِيْكُمْ وَ تَكُوْنُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ قَوْمًا صٰلِحِيْنَ‏(9)\nAQTULOOA YOOSUFA AWE’ ATRAHOOHU AARZAN YYAKHLU LAKUM WAJHUL AABEEKUM WA TAKOONOO MIN BA’DEHI QAWMAN SAALEHEENA.\n(So) Slay ye Joseph! or cast him out to some (other) land, (so that) unto you (exclusively) be the attention of your father, and ye may be after that a righteous people.\nقَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ لَا تَقْتُلُوْا يُوْسُفَ وَاَلْقُوْهُ فِىْ غَيٰبَتِ الْجُبِّ يَلْتَقِطْهُ بَعْضُ السَّيَّارَةِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(10)\nQAALA QAAELUN MINHUM LAA TAQTULOOA YOOSUFA WAALQOOHU FEE GHAYBATE AL-JUBBE YALTAQETHU BA’ZUL AS-SAYARATE IN KUNTUM FAAE’ELEENA.\nSaid a speaker among them: “Slay ye not Joseph throw him into the bottom of the well: some wayfarers may take him up; If ye must be doing it.\nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا مَا لَكَ لَا تَاْمَنَّا عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَنٰصِحُوْنَ‏(11)\nQAALOO YAABAANAA MAA LAKA LAA TAAMANNAA A’LAA YOOSUFA WA INNAA LAHU LANAASEHOONA.\nSaid they: “O’ Our father! What cause is with thee that thou dost not trust us with regard to Joseph? Verily, we are his well-wishers.\nاَرْسِلْهُ مَعَنَا غَدًا يَّرْتَعْ وَيَلْعَبْ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَحٰفِظُوْنَ‏(12)\nAARSELHU MAA’ANAA GHADAN YYARTAA’ WAYALA’AB WA INNAA LAHU LAHAAFEZOONA.\nSend him with us tomorrow that he may enjoy himself and play, and verily we for him shall be the guards.\nقَالَ اِنِّىْ لَيَحْزُنُنِىْ اَنْ تَذْهَبُوْا بِهٖ وَاَخَافُ اَنْ يَّاْكُلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَاَنْتُمْ عَنْهُ غٰفِلُوْنَ‏(13)\nQAALA INNEE LAYAHZUNUNEAA AN TAZHABOOA BEHI WA AKHAAFO AN YYAAKULAHU AZ-ZEBU WA ANTUM A’NHO GHAAFELOON.\nSaid he: “Verily it saddens me that ye should take him away, and I fear lest the wolf devour him while ye are heedless of him.\nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ اَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nQAALOO LAIL AAKALAHU AZ-ZEBU WA NAHNO U’USBATUN INNAA EZAL LLAKHAASEROONA.\nSaid they: “If the wolf were to devour while we are (so large a group) Verily then we should be losers.\nفَلَمَّا ذَهَبُوْا بِهٖ وَاَجْمَعُوْۤا اَنْ يَّجْعَلُوْهُ فِىْ غَيٰبَتِ الْجُبِّۚ وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ لَتُنَبِّئَنَّهُمْ بِاَمْرِهِمْ هٰذَا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(15)\nFALAMMAA ZAHABOOA BEHI WAAJMAU’OOA AN YYAJA’ALOOHU FEE GHAYBATE AL-JUBBE WA AWHAYNAA ELAYHE LATUNABBEANNAHUM BE-AMREHIM HAAZAA WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nSo when they had gone with him and agreed to put him in the bottom of the well, and We revealed unto him: “Thou wilt (one day) most surely tell them of this their deed while they recognise (thee) not”.\nوَجَآءُوْۤ اَبَاهُمْ عِشَآءً يَّبْكُوْنَؕ‏(16)\nWA JAAA-OO AABAAHUM E’ESHAAAN YYABKOONA.\nAnd came they unto their father at nightfall, weeping.\nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَاۤ اِنَّا ذَهَبْنَا نَسْتَبِقُ وَتَرَكْنَا يُوْسُفَ عِنْدَ مَتَاعِنَا فَاَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمُؤْمِنٍ لَّنَا وَلَوْ كُنَّا صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(17)\nQAALOO YAABAANAA INNAA ZAHABNAA NASTABEQU WATARAKNAA YOOSUFA I’NDAL MATAAE’ENAA FAAKALAHU AZ-ZEBU WA MAA ANTA BEMUMENIN LANAA WA LAW KUNNAA SAADEQEEN.\nSaid they: “O’ Our father! Verily went we racing, and left we Joseph by our things; then devoured him the wolf, but thou wilt believe us not, even if we be truthful.\nوَجَآءُوْ عَلٰى قَمِيْصِهٖ بِدَمٍ كَذِبٍؕ قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ اَنْفُسُكُمْ اَمْرًاؕ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيْلٌؕ وَاللّٰهُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلٰى مَا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(18)\nWA JAAA-OO A’LAA QAMEESEH BEDAMIN KAZEBIN QAALA BAL SAWLAT LAKUM ANFOSOKUM AAMRAN FASABRUN JAMEELUN WAL LAAHO AL-MUSTAA’AANU A’LAA MAA TASEFOONA.\nAnd came they with his shirt with false blood on it. Said he: “Nay, have beguiled you your (guilty) selves into something; But (my course is) comely patience; and God is He Whose help is to be sought against what ye describe.\nوَجَآءَتْ سَيَّارَةٌ فَاَرْسَلُوْا وَارِدَهُمْ فَاَدْلٰى دَلْوَهٗ ؕ قَالَ يٰبُشْرٰى هٰذَا غُلٰمٌ ؕ وَاَسَرُّوْهُ بِضَاعَةً  ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(19)\nWA JAAA-AT SAYARATUN FAARSALOOA WAAREDAHUM FAADLAA DALWAH QAALA YAABUSHRAA HAAZAA GHULAAMUN WAASARROOHU BEZAAA’ATAN WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BEMAA YA’MALOON.\nAnd came there a caravan and they sent their water drawer and he let down his bucket; Said (cried) he “O’ Good news!” “This is a youth!” and they concealed him as an article of merchandise; and verily God was the Knower of what all they were doing.\nوَشَرَوْهُ بِثَمَنٍۢ بَخْسٍ دَرَاهِمَ مَعْدُوْدَةٍ ۚ وَكَانُوْا فِيْهِ مِنَ الزّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(20)\nWASHARAWHU BESAMANIN BAKHSIN DARAAHEMA MAA’DOODATIN WA KAANOO FEEHE MENAL AZ-ZAAHEDEENA.\nAnd they sold him for a paltry price, for a few dirhams (silver pieces) counted out; and in him they had no interest.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِى اشْتَرٰٮهُ مِنْ مِّصْرَ لِامْرَاَتِهٖۤ اَكْرِمِىْ مَثْوٰٮهُ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّنْفَعَنَاۤ اَوْ نَتَّخِذَهٗ وَلَدًا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوْسُفَ فِى الْاَرْضِوَلِنُعَلِّمَهٗ مِنْ تَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحَادِيْثِؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَالِبٌ عَلٰٓى اَمْرِهٖ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA QAALA LAZIS TARAAHO MIN MMESRA LEAMRAATEH AAKREMEAA MASWAAHU A’SAA AN YYANFAA’ANAA AW NATTAKHEZAH LAAHO WA KAZAALEKA MAKKANNAA LEEWSUFA FIL AL-AARZEWALENUA’ALLEMAH MIN TAAWEELE AL-AAHAADEESE WAL LAAHO GHAALEBUN A’LAA AMREHI LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd he of Egypt who purchased him said unto his wife “Give him an honourable place, maybe he may profit us, or we will adopt him as a son;” And thus did We establish Joseph in the land (Egypt); and that We may teach him the interpretation of events (dreams); And Verily God is Predominant over His affair, but most of mankind know not.\nوَلَمَّا بَلَغَ اَشُدَّهٗۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُ حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(22)\nWA LAMMAA BALAGHA ASHUDDAHU AATAYNAAHO HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nAnd when he (Joseph) attained his prime (maturity) We gave him authority (apostle ship) and knowledge; And thus do We recompense the doers of good.\nوَرَاوَدَتْهُ الَّتِىْ هُوَ فِىْ بَيْتِهَا عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ وَغَلَّقَتِ الْاَبْوَابَ وَقَالَتْ هَيْتَ لَكَؕ قَالَ مَعَاذَ اللّٰهِ اِنَّهٗ رَبِّىْۤ اَحْسَنَ مَثْوَاىَؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(23)\nWARAAWADATHU LATEE HOWA FEE BAYTEHAA A’N NNAFSEH WAGHALLAQATE AL-AABWAABA WA QAALAT HAYTA LAK QAALA MAA’AAZA LAAHE INNAHU RABBEE AHSANAL MASWAAAAA INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nAnd she, in whose house he was, sought to seduce him from his (pure) self; and she fastened the doors and said: “Now come on thou! Said he: “(I seek) God’s refuge!” Verily He is my Lord! He made good my abode; Verily prosper not the unjust ones.\nوَلَقَدْ هَمَّتْ بِهٖۚ وَهَمَّ بِهَا لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ رَّاٰ بُرْهَانَ رَبِّهٖؕ كَذٰلِكَ لِنَصْرِفَ عَنْهُ السُّۤوْءَ وَالْفَحْشَآءَؕ اِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(24)\nWA LAQAD HAMMAT BEHI WAHAMMA BEHAA LAWLAA AN RRAA BURHAANA RABBEH KAZAALEKA LENASREFA A’NHO AS-SOOA WAL FAHSHAAA INNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nAnd indeed she longed for him, and he (also) would have longed for her, had he not seen the evidence of his Lord; Thus it was that We turn away from him evil and shameful deeds; Verily he was (one) of Our freed servants.\nوَاسْتَبَقَا الْبَابَ وَقَدَّتْ قَمِيْصَهٗ مِنْ دُبُرٍ وَّاَلْفَيَا سَيِّدَهَا لَدَا الْبَابِؕ قَالَتْ مَا جَزَآءُ مَنْ اَرَادَ بِاَهْلِكَ سُوْۤءًا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّسْجَنَ اَوْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(25)\nWAASTABAQAA BAABA WAQADDAT QAMEESAH MIN DUBURIN WWAALFAYAA SAYDAHAA LADAA AL-BAABE QAALAT MAA JAZAAA-O MAN ARAADA BEAAHLEKA SOOAN ILLAA AN YYUSJANA AW A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nAnd raced they both to the door, and she rent his shirt from behind and they met her husband at the door. She said (cried); “What is the punishment for him who intendeth evil to thy wife save he be imprisoned or a painful torment?\nقَالَ هِىَ رَاوَدَتْنِىْ عَنْ نَّفْسِىْ وَشَهِدَ شَاهِدٌ مِّنْ اَهْلِهَاۚ اِنْ كَانَ قَمِيْصُهٗ قُدَّ مِنْ قُبُلٍ فَصَدَقَتْ وَهُوَ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALA HEYA RAAWADATNEAA A’N NNAFSEAA WA SHAHEDA SHAAHEDUN MIN AHLEHAA IN KAANA QAMEESUH QUDDA MIN QUBULIN FASADAQAT WA HOWA MENAL KAAZEBEEN.\nHe said: “She (it was who) sought to seduce me from my (pure) self” and bore witness, a witness of her own household; “If his shirt be rent from the front, she speaketh the truth and he is of the liars.\nوَاِنْ كَانَ قَمِيْصُهٗ قُدَّ مِنْ دُبُرٍ فَكَذَبَتْ وَهُوَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(27)\nWA KAANA QAMEESUH QUDDA MIN DUBURIN FAKAZABAT WA HOWA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nAnd if his shirt be rent from behind, she sayeth a lie and he is of the truthful Ones.\nفَلَمَّا رَاٰ قَمِيْصَهٗ قُدَّ مِنْ دُبُرٍ قَالَ اِنَّهٗ مِنْ كَيْدِكُنَّؕ اِنَّ كَيْدَكُنَّ عَظِيْمٌ‏(28)\nFALAMMAA RAA QAMEESAH QUDDA MIN DUBURIN QAALA INNAHU MIN KAYDEKUNNA INNAL KAYDAKUNNA A’ZEEM.\nSo when he (the husband) saw the shirt rent from behind, said he: “Verily it is a guile of ye women! Verily great is your guile!\nيُوْسُفُ اَعْرِضْ عَنْ هٰذَا وَاسْتَغْفِرِىْ لِذَنْۢبِكِ ۖ ۚ اِنَّكِ كُنْتِ مِنَ الْخٰطِٮئِيْنَ‏(29)\nYOOSUFU AAA’REZ A’N HAAZAA WAASTAGHFEREAA LEZANBEKE AENNAKE KUNTE MENAL AL-KHAATEEENA.\nO’ Joseph! Leave thou this affair, and thou (O’ my wife!) ask forgiveness for thy sin; Verily thou art of the guilty (ones).\nوَقَالَ نِسْوَةٌ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ امْرَاَتُ الْعَزِيْزِ تُرَاوِدُ فَتٰٮهَا عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖۚ قَدْ شَغَفَهَا حُبًّا ؕ اِنَّا لَنَرٰٮهَا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(30)\nWA QAALA NESWATUN FIL MADEENATE AMRAATU A’ZEEZIL TURAAWEDU FATAAHAA A’N NNAFSEH QAD SHAGHAFAHAA HUBBAL INNAA LANARAAHAA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nAnd said the women in the City: “The wife of the (great) ‘Aziz’ (the chief) seeketh to seduce her slave from his (pure) self; Verily hath he affected her deeply with love; Verily we see her in manifest error.\nفَلَمَّا سَمِعَتْ بِمَكْرِهِنَّ اَرْسَلَتْ اِلَيْهِنَّ وَاَعْتَدَتْ لَهُنَّ مُتَّكَاً وَّاٰتَتْ كُلَّ وَاحِدَةٍ مِّنْهُنَّ سِكِّيْنًا وَّقَالَتِ اخْرُجْ عَلَيْهِنَّ ۚ فَلَمَّا رَاَيْنَهٗۤ اَكْبَرْنَهٗ وَقَطَّعْنَ اَيْدِيَهُنَّ وَقُلْنَ حَاشَ لِلّٰهِ مَا هٰذَا بَشَرًا ؕ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا مَلَكٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(31)\nFALAMMAA SAMEA’AT BEMAKREHENNA AARSALAT AELAYHENNA WAAA’TADAT LAHUNNA MUTTAKAA WWAATAT KULLA WAAHEDATIN MIN-HUNNA SEKKEENAN WA QAALATIN AKHRUJ A’LAYHINNA FALAMMAA RAAYNAH AAKBARNAH WAQATTAA’NA AAYDEEHUNNA WAQULNA HAASHA LILLAAHE MAA HAAZAA BASHARAN IN HAAZAA ILLAA MALAKUN KAREEM.\nAnd when she heard of their scheming talk, she sent for them, and prepared for them a repast and gave unto each one of them a knife and said (unto Joseph) “Come thou out unto them.” So when they saw him, they did extol him; and (in their amazement) cut their hands, and said (exclaimed): “Hasha-lillah!” (Far from God is every imperfection!) This is not a mortal (human being), This is none but a noble angel!\nقَالَتْ فَذٰلِكُنَّ الَّذِىْ لُمْتُنَّنِىْ فِيْهِؕ وَ لَقَدْ رَاوَدْتُّهٗ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ فَاسْتَعْصَمَؕ وَلَئِنْ لَّمْ يَفْعَلْ مَاۤ اٰمُرُهٗ لَيُسْجَنَنَّ وَلَيَكُوْنًا مِّنَ الصّٰغِرِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALAT FAZAALEKUNNA LAZEE LUMTUNNANEAA FEEH WA LAQAD RAAWADTTUH A’N NNAFSEH FAASTAA’SAMA WA LAIN LAM YAFA’AL MAA AAAMURUH LAYUSJANANNA WALAYAKOONAN MENAL AS-SAAGHEREENA.\nSaid she: “This is he about whom ye blamed me; and indeed I sought to seduce him from his (pure) self, but he did firmly abstain himself guiltless; and (now) if he doth not what I bid him, he shall certainly be imprisoned, and he shall certainly be of those brought low!\nقَالَ رَبِّ السِّجْنُ اَحَبُّ اِلَىَّ مِمَّا يَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَيْهِۚ وَاِلَّا تَصْرِفْ عَنِّىْ كَيْدَهُنَّ اَصْبُ اِلَيْهِنَّ وَاَكُنْ مِّنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(33)\nQAALA RABBE AS-SEJNU AAHABBU ELAYYA MIMMAA YADU’OONANEAA ELAYHE WA ILLAA TASREF A’NNEE KAYDAHUNNA AASBU AELAYHENNA WA AKUM MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nSaid he “O’ my Lord! The prison is dearer to me than that unto which they invite me; and if thou turneth not away from me their guile I may yearn unto them and become of the ignorant ones.\nفَاسْتَجَابَ لَهٗ رَبُّهٗ فَصَرَفَ عَنْهُ كَيْدَهُنَّؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(34)\nFAASTAJAABA LAHU RABBOHU FASARAFA A’NHO KAYDAHUNNA INNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nThereupon heard him his Lord and turned He away their guile from him; Verily He is the All Hearing, The All-Knowing.\nثُمَّ بَدَا لَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا رَاَوُا الْاٰيٰتِ لَيَسْجُنُنَّهٗ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(35)\nSUMMA BADAA LAHUM MIN BA’DE MAA RAAWUA AAYAATE LAYASJUNUNNAH HATTAA HEEN.\nThen it occurred to them (even) after they had seen the signs (of his innocence) that they should imprison him for a time.\nوَدَخَلَ مَعَهُ السِّجْنَ فَتَيٰنِؕ قَالَ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮنِىْۤ اَعْصِرُ خَمْرًا ۚ وَقَالَ الْاٰخَرُ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮنِىْۤ اَحْمِلُ فَوْقَ رَاْسِىْ خُبْزًا تَاْكُلُ الطَّيْرُ مِنْهُ ؕ نَبِّئْنَا بِتَاْوِيْلِهٖ ۚ اِنَّا نَرٰٮكَ مِنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(36)\nWA DAKHALAL MAA’AHU AS-SEJNA FATAYNE QAALA AAHADUHUMAA INNEE AARAANEAA AAA’SERU KHAMRAN WA QAALA AL-AAAKHARU INNEE AARAANEAA AAHMELU FAWQA RAASEAA KHUBZAN TAAKULU AT-TAYRU MINHO NABBENAA BETAAWEELEH INNAA NARAAKA MENAL MOHSENEEN.\nAnd with him entered the prison, two youths; Said one of them (Unto Joseph) “Verily I saw (in dream) myself pressing wine.” And said the other: “I saw (in dream) myself carrying bread on my head, and birds eating there of. Inform us of its interpretation: Verily we see thee of the doers of good (to all).\nقَالَ لَا يَاْتِيْكُمَا طَعَامٌ تُرْزَقٰنِهٖۤ اِلَّا نَبَّاْتُكُمَا بِتَاْوِيْلِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَكُمَا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمَا مِمَّا عَلَّمَنِىْ رَبِّىْ ؕ اِنِّىْ تَرَكْتُ مِلَّةَ قَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(37)\nQAALA LAA YAATEEKUMAA TA-A’AMUN TURZAQAANEH ILLAA NABBAATUKUMAA BETAAWEELEH QABLA AN YYAATEEKUMAA ZAA LEKUMAA MIMMAA A’ALLAMANEAA RABBEE INNEE TARAKTU MILLATA QAWMIN LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM KAAFEROON.\nSaid he (Joseph): “There shall not come unto you the food which ye are fed with but I inform ye two of its interpretation before it cometh unto ye two; This is of what my Lord hath taught me; Verily I have forsaken the religion of the people who believe not in God, and of the hereafter, they are dis believers.\nوَاتَّبَعْتُ مِلَّةَ اٰبَآءِىْۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَؕ مَا كَانَ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نُّشْرِكَ بِاللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍؕ ذٰلِكَ مِنْ فَضْلِ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْنَا وَعَلَى النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(38)\nWAATTABAA’TU MILLATA AAABAAEAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISHAAQA WAYAA’QOOBA MAA KAANA LANAA AN NNUSHREKA BIL-LAAHE MIN SHAYIN ZAALEKA MIN FAZLIL LAAHE A’LAYNAA WA NAASE LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YASHKOROON.\nAnd I follow the religion of my fathers Abraham, Isaac and Jacob; and it is not (lawful) for us to associate aught with God; This is by God’s grace upon us and on mankind, but most people give not thanks.\nيٰصَاحِبَىِ السِّجْنِ ءَاَرْبَابٌ مُّتَفَرِّقُوْنَ خَيْرٌ اَمِ اللّٰهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُؕ‏(39)\nYAASAAHEBAA AS-SEJNE AARBAABUN MMUTAFARREQOONA KHAYRUL AMIL LAAHO AL-WAAHEDU AL-QAHHAARU.\nO’ my (two) fellows of the prison! Are (many) lords differing from each other better or God the One, the All-Dominant?\nمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَآءً سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍؕ اِنِ الْحُكْمُ اِلَّا لِلّٰهِؕ اَمَرَ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُؕ ذٰلِكَ الدِّيْنُ الْقَيِّمُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(40)\nMAA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONEHI ILLAA AASMAAAN SAMMAYTUMOOHAA ANTUM WA AAABAAUKUM MAA ANZALAL LAAHO BEHAA MIN SULTAANIN ENIS HUKMO ILLAA LIL-LAAH AMARAL ALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA AEEAHU ZAALEKA DEENO AL-QAYMU LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nYe worship not besides Him but (mere) names which ye have named, ye and your fathers, God hath not sent down for them any authority; there is no judgment but God’s; He hath bidden that ye worship not but unto Him; This is the right religion, but most people know (it) not.\nيٰصَاحِبَىِ السِّجْنِ اَمَّاۤ اَحَدُكُمَا فَيَسْقِىْ رَبَّهٗ خَمْرًاۚ وَاَمَّا الْاٰخَرُ فَيُصْلَبُ فَتَاْكُلُ الطَّيْرُ مِنْ رَّاْسِهٖؕ قُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ تَسْتَفْتِيٰنِؕ‏(41)\nYAASAAHEBAA AS-SEJNE AMMAA AAHADUKUMAA FAYASQEAA WAL KHAMRAN WA AMMAA AL-AAAKHARU FAYUSLABU FATAAKULU AT-TAYRU MIN RRAASEH QUZEAAA MIN LAZEE FEEHE TASTAFTEENE.\nO’ my (two) fellows of the prison! As to one of you, he will pour out wine for his lord to drink; As for the other, he shall be crucified, so that the birds shall eat from his head. The matter is decreed about which ye two inquired.\nوَقَالَ لِلَّذِىْ ظَنَّ اَنَّهٗ نَاجٍ مِّنْهُمَا اذْكُرْنِىْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ فَاَنْسٰٮهُ الشَّيْطٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهٖ فَلَبِثَ فِى السِّجْنِ بِضْعَ سِنِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA QAALA LIL-LAZEE ZANNAS ANNAHU NAAJIN MINHOMAA WA AZKURNEAA I’NDAL RABBEKA FAANSAAHU SHAYTAANO ZEKRA RABBEHI QAWMEHI FIL AS-SEJNE BEZA’A SENEEN.\nAnd he said unto him whom he knew would be delivered of the two: “mention me unto thy lord;” But the devil caused him to forget mentioning (it) to his lord, so he remained in the prison a few years (more).\nوَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى سَبْعَ بَقَرٰتٍ سِمَانٍ يَّاْكُلُهُنَّ سَبْعٌ عِجَافٌ وَّسَبْعَ سُنْۢبُلٰتٍ خُضْرٍ وَّاُخَرَ يٰبِسٰتٍؕ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَاُ اَفْتُوْنِىْ فِىْ رُءْيَاىَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ لِلرُّءْيَا تَعْبُرُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA QAALA AL-MALEKU INNEE AARAA SAB-A’ BAQARAATIN SEMAANIN YYAAKULUHUNNA SABA’UN E’EJAAFUN WWASABA’A SUNBULAATIN KHUZRINW WWAAKHARA YAABESAATIN YAA AYYOHAL MALA-O AFTOONEE FEE RUYAAAAA IN KUNTUM LELRRUYAA TAA’BUROONA.\nAnd said the king “Verily, I did see in (dream) seven fat kine which seven lean ones devoured, and seven green ears and (seven) others dry; O’ chiefs (of my court)! Explain ye unto me my dream, if ye can interpret a dream.\nقَالُوْۤا اَضْغَاثُ اَحْلَامٍۚ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِتَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحْلَامِ بِعٰلِمِيْنَ‏(44)\nQAALOO AAZGHAASU AAHLAAMIN WA MAA NAHNO BETAAWEELE AL-AAHLAAME BEA’AALEMEENA.\nSaid they: “Confused dreams (are these)! and we know not the interpretation of such (confused) dreams.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْ نَجَا مِنْهُمَا وَادَّكَرَ بَعْدَ اُمَّةٍ اَنَا اُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِتَاْوِيْلِهٖ فَاَرْسِلُوْنِ‏(45)\nWA QAALA LAZEE NAJAA MINHOMAA WAADDAKARA BA’DA UMMATIN ANAA AUNABBEUKUM BETAAWEELEH FAARSELOONE.\nAnd said he of the two who had been released, and re membered after a long time; “I will expound unto you its interpretation, so let me go (to the prison).\nيُوْسُفُ اَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيْقُ اَ فْتِنَا فِىْ سَبْعِ بَقَرٰتٍ سِمَانٍ يَّاْكُلُهُنَّ سَبْعٌ عِجَافٌ وَّسَبْعِ سُنْۢبُلٰتٍ خُضْرٍ وَّاُخَرَ يٰبِسٰتٍ ۙ لَّعَلِّىْۤ اَرْجِعُ اِلَى النَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(46)\nYOOSUFU AYYOHAL AS-SEDDEEQU A’ZAABAN FTENAA FEE SABE’E BAQARAATIN SEMAANIN YYAAKULUHUNNA SABA’UN E’EJAAFUN WWASABE’E SUNBULAATIN KHUZRINW WWAAKHARA YAABESAATIN LA-A’LLEE AARJEU’U ELAL NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YA’LAMOON.\nJoseph! O’ truthful one! expound thou unto us seven fat kine which seven lean ones devour, and seven ears green and seven (others) dry, that I may return unto the people so that they may know.\nقَالَ تَزْرَعُوْنَ سَبْعَ سِنِيْنَ دَاَبًاۚ فَمَا حَصَدْتُّمْ فَذَرُوْهُ فِىْ سُنْۢبُلِهٖۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّمَّا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(47)\nQAALA TAZRAU’OONA SAB-A’ SENEEN DAABAN FAMAA HASADTTUM FAZAROOHU FEE SUNBULEH ILLAA QALEELAA MIMMAA TAAKULOONA.\nSaid he: “Ye shall sow seven years as usual, but that which ye reap leave ye in its ears, except a little of which ye eat.\nثُمَّ يَاْتِىْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ سَبْعٌ شِدَادٌ يَّاْكُلْنَ مَا قَدَّمْتُمْ لَهُنَّ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّمَّا تُحْصِنُوْنَ‏(48)\nSUMMA YAATEE MIN BA’DE ZAALEKA SABA’UN SHEDAADUN YYAAKULNA MAA QADDAMTUM LAHUNNA ILLAA QALEELAA MIMMAA TUHSENOONA.\nThen shall come after that seven years of hardship (famine), which shall eat away all that ye have laid by beforehand for them, except a little of which ye have preserved.\nثُمَّ يَاْتِىْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ عَامٌ فِيْهِ يُغَاثُ النَّاسُ وَفِيْهِ يَعْصِرُوْنَ‏(49)\nSUMMA YAATEE MIN BA’DE ZAALEKA A’AAMUN FEEHE YUGHAASU NAASO WA FEEHE YAA’SEROONA.\nThen will come after that a year people will have abundant rain and in having it they will press wine.\nوَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِهٖۚ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُ الرَّسُوْلُ قَالَ ارْجِعْ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فَسْئَلْهُ مَا بَالُ النِّسْوَةِ الّٰتِىْ قَطَّعْنَ اَيْدِيَهُنَّؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ بِكَيْدِهِنَّ عَلِيْمٌ‏(50)\nWA QAALA AL-MALEKU ATOONEAA BEHI FALAMMAA JAAA-AHUL RASOOLO QAALA ARJEA’ ELAA RABBEKA FASALHU MAA BAALU AN-NESWATE KHAALEKA QATTAA’NA AAYDEEHUNNA INNAL RABBEE BEKAYDEHENNA A’LEEM.\nAnd said the king: “Bring him unto me!” So when the messenger came unto him, said he (Joseph): “Go thou back unto thy lord and ask him, what is the matter with the women who cut their hands; Verily my Lord knoweth their guile.\nقَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُنَّ اِذْ رَاوَدْتُّنَّ يُوْسُفَ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖؕ قُلْنَ حَاشَ لِلّٰهِ مَا عَلِمْنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنْ سُوْۤءٍ ؕ قَالَتِ امْرَاَتُ الْعَزِيْزِ الْئٰنَ حَصْحَصَ الْحَقُّ اَنَا رَاوَدْتُّهٗ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ وَاِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(51)\nQAALA MAA KHATBUKUNNA IZ RAAWADTTUNNA YOOSUFA A’N NNAFSEH QULNA HAASHA LILLAAHE MAA A’LIMNAA A’LAYHE MIN SOOIN QAALATE AMRAATU A’ZEEZIL AL-AANA HASHASA HAQQO ANAA RAAWADTTUH A’N NNAFSEH WA INNAHU LAMENAS SAADEQEENA.\nSaid the king (unto the women) what was the matter with you when ye sought to seduce Joseph from his (pure) self?” Said (replied) the women! “Hasha-lillah (Far from God is every imperfection) we know not any evil against him!” Said the Aziz’s wife: “Now the truth hath become manifest, I (it was who) sought to seduce him from his (pure) self; And verily he is of the truthful ones!\nذٰ لِكَ لِيَعْلَمَ اَنِّىْ لَمْ اَخُنْهُ بِالْغَيْبِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ كَيْدَ الْخَآئِنِيْنَ‏(52)\nZAA LEKA LEEA’LAMA AANNEAA LAM AAKHUNHU BIL-GHAYBE WA ANNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE KAYDA AL-KHAAENEENA.\n(Said Joseph) This (Inquiry I caused) that he (the King) might know that I have not been unfaithful unto him in his absence, and that God guideth not the guile of the unfaithful ones.\nوَمَاۤ اُبَرِّئُ نَفْسِىْۚ اِنَّ النَّفْسَ لَاَمَّارَةٌۢ بِالسُّوْٓءِ اِلَّا مَا رَحِمَ رَبِّىْ ؕاِنَّ رَبِّىْ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(53)\nWA MAA AUBARREU NAFSEE INNAL AN-NAFSA LAAMMAARATUN BIS-SOOO-E ILLAA MAA RAHEMA RABBEE AENNA RABBEE GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nI exculpate not myself, verily (one’s) self is wont to bid (him to) evil, except such as my Lord hath had mercy on; Verily my Lord is Oft-Forgiving, All- Merciful.\nوَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِهٖۤ اَسْتَخْلِصْهُ لِنَفْسِىْۚ فَلَمَّا كَلَّمَهٗ قَالَ اِنَّكَ الْيَوْمَ لَدَيْنَا مَكِيْنٌ اَمِيْنٌ‏(54)\nWA QAALA AL-MALEKU ATOONEAA BEHI AASTAKHLESHU LE-NAFSEE FALAMMAA KALLAMAH QAALA INNAKA YAWMA LADAYNAA MAKEENUN AMEEN.\nAnd the king said (Ordered) “Bring him unto me, I will exclude him for (service to) my (own) self!” So when he had spoken unto him: he (the king) said: “Verily thou art (from) this day in our (own) presence, accommodated (honourably) (as) a Trusted one!\nقَالَ اجْعَلْنِىْ عَلٰى خَزَآئِنِ الْاَرْضِۚ اِنِّىْ حَفِيْظٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(55)\nQAALA AJA’ALNEAA A’LAA KHAZAAENE ARZE INNEE HAFEEZUN A’LEEM.\nSaid he: “Set me (in authority) over the treasuries of the land; Verily I am a (faithful) keeper, knowing well (its management).\nوَكَذٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوْسُفَ فِى الْاَرْضِۚ يَتَبَوَّاُ مِنْهَا حَيْثُ يَشَآءُ ؕ نُصِيْبُ بِرَحْمَتِنَا مَنْ نَّشَآءُۚ وَلَا نُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(56)\nWA KAZAALEKA MAKKANNAA LEEWSUFA FIL ARZE YATABAWAU MINHAA HAYSO YASHAAA NUSEEBU BERAHMATENAA MAN NNASHAAU WA LAA NUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nThus We did establish Joseph in the land; to take possession therein as he pleased; We do bestow Our mercy on whomsoever We will, and We waste not the recompense of the doers of good.\nوَلَاَجْرُ الْاٰخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَكَانُوْا يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(57)\nWALAAJRU AAKHERATE KHAYRUL LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO WA KAANOO YATTAQOON.\nAnd certainly the recompense of the hereafter is (much) better for those who believe and guard (themselves) against evil.\nوَجَآءَ اِخْوَةُ يُوْسُفَ فَدَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَعَرَفَهُمْ وَهُمْ لَهٗ مُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA JAAA-A AEKHWATU YOOSUFA FA DAKHALOO A’LAYHE FAA’ARAFAHUM WA HUM LAHU MUNKEROONA.\nAnd came the brothers of Joseph and entered they unto him, and he knew them but they knew him not.\nوَ لَمَّا جَهَّزَهُمْ بِجَهَازِهِمْ قَالَ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِاَخٍ لَّكُمْ مِّنْ اَبِيْكُمْۚ اَلَا تَرَوْنَ اَنِّىْۤ اُوْفِی الْكَيْلَ وَاَنَا خَيْرُ الْمُنْزِلِيْنَ‏(59)\nWA LAMMAA JAHHAZAHUM BEJAHAAZEHEM QAALA ATOONEAA BEAAKHIN LAKUM MIN AABEEKUM ALAA TARAWNA AANNEAA AOOFE AL-KAYLA ANAT KHAYRUR AL-MUNZELEENA.\nAnd when he hath furnished them with their provision, said he (unto them): “Bring ye unto me a brother of yours from your father; See ye not that I give full measure? and that I am the best of hosts?\nفَاِنْ لَّمْ تَاْتُوْنِىْ بِهٖ فَلَا كَيْلَ لَكُمْ عِنْدِىْ وَلَا تَقْرَبُوْنِ‏(60)\nFA-IN LAM TAATOONEAA BEHI FALAA KAYLA LAKUM E’ENDEAA WA LAA TAQRABOONE.\nBut if ye bring him not unto me, then there shall be no measure (of corn) for you with me, nor shall ye (even) come near me.\nقَالُوْا سَنُرَاوِدُ عَنْهُ اَبَاهُ وَاِنَّا لَفَاعِلُوْنَ‏(61)\nQAALOO SANURAAWEDU A’NHO AABAAHU WA INNAA LAFAAE’ELOONA.\nThey said: “We will seek to get him from his father, and verily We certainly shall do it.\nوَقَالَ لِفِتْيٰنِهِ اجْعَلُوْا بِضَاعَتَهُمْ فِىْ رِحَالِهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَعْرِفُوْنَهَاۤ اِذَا انْقَلَبُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA QAALA LEFETYAANEHE AJA’ALOOA BEZAAA’ATAHUM FEE REHAALEHEM LA-A’LLAHUM YAA’REFOONAHAA EZAA QALABOO ELAA AHLEHIM LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd said he unto his servants: “Put their goods into their saddle-bags that they may perceive it when they return unto their family, so that they may come back.\nفَلَمَّا رَجَعُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَبِيْهِمْ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا مُنِعَ مِنَّا الْكَيْلُ فَاَرْسِلْ مَعَنَاۤ اَخَانَا نَكْتَلْ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَحٰفِظُوْنَ‏(63)\nFALAMMAA RAJAU’OOA ELAA AABEEHEM QAALOO YAABAANAA MUNEA’A MINNAA AL-KAYLU FAARSEL MAA’ANAA AAKHAANAA NAKTAL WA INNAA LAHU LAHAAFEZOONA.\nSo when they returned unto their father, said they: “O’ our father! The measure is denied unto us, so send with us our brother, so that we may get the measure: And verily, certainly we will we guard him (well).\nقَالَ هَلْ اٰمَنُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اِلَّا كَمَاۤ اَمِنْتُكُمْ عَلٰٓى اَخِيْهِ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ فَاللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ حٰفِظًا وَّهُوَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(64)\nQAALA HAL AAAMANUKUM A’LAYHE ILLAA KAMAA AAMENTUKUM A’LAA AKHEEHE MIN QABL WA FAL-LAAHO KHAYRUL HAAFEZAN WA AARHAMU AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nHe said: “Can I trust him unto you except as I entrusted his brother unto you aforetime? but God is the Best Guard, and He is the Most Merciful of the merciful ones.\nوَلَمَّا فَتَحُوْا مَتَاعَهُمْ وَجَدُوْا بِضَاعَتَهُمْ رُدَّتْ اِلَيْهِمْؕ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا مَا نَبْغِىْؕ هٰذِهٖ بِضَاعَتُنَا رُدَّتْ اِلَيْنَا ۚ وَنَمِيْرُ اَهْلَنَا وَنَحْفَظُ اَخَانَا وَنَزْدَادُ كَيْلَ بَعِيْرٍؕ ذٰ لِكَ كَيْلٌ يَّسِيْرٌ‏(65)\nWA LAMMAA FATAHOOA MATAAA’AHUM WAJADOOA BEZAAA’ATAHUM RUDDAT AELAYHEM QAALOO YAABAANAA MAA NABGHEAA HAAZEHI BEZAAA’ATUNAA RUDDAT ELAYNAA WANAMEERU AAHLANAA WANAHFAZU AAKHAANAA WANAZDAADU KAYLA BAE’EERIN ZAA LEKA KAYLUN YYASEERUN.\nAnd when they opened their belongings, they found their goods returned unto them. Said they: “O’ our father! What (more) can we desire? This our goods hath been returned unto us; and we will bring (more) corn for our family and guard our brother, and we shall have in addition the measure of a camel (load); This (what we have now brought) is (only) an easy measure.\nقَالَ لَنْ اُرْسِلَهٗ مَعَكُمْ حَتّٰى تُؤْتُوْنِ مَوْثِقًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ لَتَاْتُنَّنِىْ بِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّحَاطَ بِكُمْۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اٰتَوْهُ مَوْثِقَهُمْ قَالَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَا نَقُوْلُ وَكِيْلٌ‏(66)\nQAALA LAN AURSELAH MA-A’KUM HATTAA TUTOONE MAWSEQAN MENAL LAAHE LATAATUNNANEAA BEHI ILLAA AN YYUHAATA BEKUM FALAMMAA AAATAWHU MAWSEQAHUM QAALA LAAHO A’LAA MAA NAQOOLU WAKEELUN.\nSaid (Jacob) “Never will I send him with you until ye pledge a firm covenant in God’s name that ye will most surely bring him back unto me, unless ye are completely surrounded; And when pledged they unto him a covenant, said he: (There is) God over all what we say, a Guardian-Witness.\nوَقَالَ يٰبَنِىَّ لَا تَدْخُلُوْا مِنْۢ بَابٍ وَّاحِدٍ وَّادْخُلُوْا مِنْ اَبْوَابٍ مُّتَفَرِّقَةٍؕ وَمَاۤ اُغْنِىْ عَنْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍؕ اِنِ الْحُكْمُ اِلَّا لِلّٰهِؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُۚ وَعَلَيْهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُتَوَكِّلُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA QAALA BANIYYA LAA LAA MIN BAABIN WAAHEDIN WWAADKHULOOA MIN AABWAABIN MMUTAFARREQATIN WA MAA AUGHNEAA A’NKUM MENAL LAAHE MIN SHAYIN ENIS HUKMO ILLAA LIL-LAAH A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA A’LAYHE FALYATAWAKKALE AL-MUTAWAKKELOONA.\nAnd said he: “O’ my sons! Enter ye not by one gate, but enter ye by different gates; and I cannot avail you aught against God; judgment is only God’s; On Him do I rely; and on Him (only) let the reliants rely.\nوَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا مِنْ حَيْثُ اَمَرَهُمْ اَبُوْهُمْ ؕمَا كَانَ يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّا حَاجَةً فِىْ نَفْسِ يَعْقُوْبَ قَضٰٮهَاؕ وَاِنَّهٗ لَذُوْ عِلْمٍ لِّمَا عَلَّمْنٰهُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA LAMMAA DAKHALOO MIN HAYSO AAMARAHUM AABOOHUM MAA KAANA YUGHNEE A’NHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA HAAJATAM FEE NAFSE YA’QOOBAL QAZAAHAA WA INNAHU LAZOO I’LMIN LEMAA A’LLAMNAAHUSH-SHE’RA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd when they had entered as they were bidden by their father; it did not avail them aught against (the decree of) God; but (it was only) a desire in Jacob’s soul which he satisfied; and verily, he was possessed of knowledge for we had taught him, but most people know (this) not.\nوَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ اٰوٰٓى اِلَيْهِ اَخَاهُ قَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اَنَا اَخُوْكَ فَلَا تَبْتَئِسْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(69)\nWA LAMMAA DAKHALOO A’LAA YOOSUFA AAAWAAA ELAYHE AAKHAAHU QAALA INNEE ANAA AAKHOOKA FALAA TABTAES BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAnd when they entered in unto Joseph, he lodged his (own) brother (Benjamin) with himself, said (into his ears) “I am thy brother (Joseph), therefore grieve thou not at what they do.\nفَلَمَّا جَهَّزَهُمْ بِجَهَازِهِمْ جَعَلَ السِّقَايَةَ فِىْ رَحْلِ اَخِيْهِ ثُمَّ اَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ اَ يَّتُهَا الْعِيْرُ اِنَّكُمْ لَسَارِقُوْنَ‏(70)\nFALAMMAA JAHHAZAHUM BEJAHAAZEHEM JA-A’LA AS-SEQAAYATA FEE RAHLE AKHEEHE SUMMA AAZZANA MUAZZENUN A’ZAABAN YYATUHAA AL-E’EERU INNAKUM LASAAREQOONA.\nAnd when he had furnished them with their provisions, (at the instance of Joseph) was placed the drinking cup in his brother’s saddle-bag; Then cried out a crier: “O’ ye (of) the caravan! Verily ye are thieves!\nقَالُوْا وَاَقْبَلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّاذَا تَفْقِدُوْنَ‏(71)\nQAALOO WAAQBALOOA A’LAYHIM MMAAZAA TAFQEDOONA.\nSaid they, while turning unto them: “What is it that ye miss?\nقَالُوْا نَفْقِدُ صُوَاعَ الْمَلِكِ وَلِمَنْ جَآءَ بِهٖ حِمْلُ بَعِيْرٍ وَّاَنَا بِهٖ زَعِيْمٌ‏(72)\nQAALOO NAFQEDU SOOAA’A MALEKIL WA LEMAN JAAA-A BEHI HEMLU BAE’EERIN WWAANAA BEHI ZAE’EEMUN.\nSaid they: “We miss the king’s drinking cup and whosoever bringeth it, shall have a camel load (of corn); and I am responsible for it.\nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتُمْ مَّا جِئْنَا لِنُفْسِدَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا كُنَّا سَارِقِيْنَ‏(73)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE LAQAD A’ALEMTUM MAA JENAA LENUFSEDA FIL ARZE WA MAA KUNNAA SAAREQEENA.\nSaid they: “By God! Ye know that we came not to make mischief in the land, and nor we are thieves.\nقَالُوْا فَمَا جَزَاۤؤُهٗۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ كٰذِبِيْنَ‏(74)\nQAALOO FAMAA JAZAAUH IN KUNTUM KAAZEBEENA.\nThey said: “But what shall be the punishment for this, if ye be liars?\nقَالُوْا جَزَاۤؤُهٗ مَنْ وُّجِدَ فِىْ رَحْلِهٖ فَهُوَ جَزَاۤؤُهٗؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(75)\nQAALOO JAZAAUH MAN WWUJEDA FEE RAHLEH FAHOWA JAZAAUH KAZAALEKA NAJZIL ZAALEMEEN.\nSaid they: “The punishment for it shall be that he in whose bag it is found shall himself be (held as bondsman) in penalty for it; Thus do we punish the wrong-doers.\nفَبَدَاَ بِاَوْعِيَتِهِمْ قَبْلَ وِعَآءِ اَخِيْهِ ثُمَّ اسْتَخْرَجَهَا مِنْ وِّعَآءِ اَخِيْهِؕ كَذٰلِكَ كِدْنَا لِيُوْسُفَؕ مَا كَانَ لِيَاْخُذَ اَخَاهُ فِىْ دِيْنِ الْمَلِكِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ نَرْفَعُ دَرَجٰتٍ مَّنْ نَّشَآءُؕ وَفَوْقَ كُلِّ ذِىْ عِلْمٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(76)\nFABADAA BEAAWE’EETEHEM QABLA WEA’AAE AKHEEHE SUMMA ASTAKHRAJAHAA MIN WWEA’AAE AAKHEEHE KAZAALEKA KEDNAA LEEWSUFA MAA KAANA LEEAKHUZA AAKHAAHU FEE DEEN MALEKIL ILLAA AN YASHAAA-ALLAAH NARFAU’U DARAJAATIN MAN NNASHAAU WA FAWQA KULLE ZEE I’LMIN A’LEEM.\nThen he (Joseph) began (the search) with their sacks before the sack of his brother, then he drew it out from his brother’s sack; Thus did We plan for Joseph; it was not (lawful) that he should take his brother under the king’s law unless God willed it; We raise the degrees (of wisdom and knowledge) whomsoever We will; and above every one endued with knowledge is the All-Knowing (One).\nقَالُوْۤا اِنْ يَّسْرِقْ فَقَدْ سَرَقَ اَخٌ لَّهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُ ۚ فَاَسَرَّهَا يُوْسُفُ فِىْ نَفْسِهٖ وَلَمْ يُبْدِهَا لَهُمْ ۚ قَالَ اَنْتُمْ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا ۚ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(77)\nQAALOO IN YYASREQ FAQAD SARAQA AAKHUN LAHU MIN QABLO FAASARRAHAA YOOSUFU FEE WA WA LAM YUBDEHAA LAHUM QAALA ANTUM HOWA MMAKAANAN WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA TASEFOONA.\nThey said: If he stealeth, indeed did steal before, a brother of his, but Joseph kept it a secret to himself, and disclosed it not unto them; he said: “Ye are in an evil condition, and God knoweth best what ye allege.\nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْعَزِيْزُ اِنَّ لَهٗۤ اَبًا شَيْخًا كَبِيْرًا فَخُذْ اَحَدَنَا مَكَانَهٗۚ اِنَّا نَرٰٮكَ مِنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(78)\nQAALOO YAA AYYOHAL A’ZEEZUL INNAL LAHU AABAN SHAYKHAN KABEERAA FA-KHUZ AAHADANAA MAKAANAHU INNAA NARAAKA MENAL MOHSENEEN.\nSaid they: “O’ Aziz! he hath a father, a very old (who loveth him very much), so take one of us in his place; Verily we see thee of the doers of good (to others).\nقَالَ مَعَاذَ اللّٰهِ اَنْ نَّاْخُذَ اِلَّا مَنْ وَّجَدْنَا مَتَاعَنَا عِنْدَهٗۤ ۙ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(79)\nQAALA MAA’AAZA LAAHE AN NNAAKHUZA ILLAA MAN WWAJADNAA MATAAA’ANAA I’NDAHU INNAA EZAL LLAZAALEMOONA.\nSaid he “God protect us! (from acting a forbidden deed) that we should seize (any one) other than him with whom found we our property, for verily then we would be of the unjust ones.\nفَلَمَّا اسْتَايْئَسُوْا مِنْهُ خَلَصُوْا نَجِيًّا ؕ قَالَ كَبِيْرُهُمْ اَلَمْ تَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اَبَاكُمْ قَدْ اَخَذَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَّوْثِقًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَمِنْ قَبْلُ مَا فَرَّطْتُّمْ فِىْ يُوْسُفَ ۚ فَلَنْ اَبْرَحَ الْاَرْضَ حَتّٰى يَاْذَنَ لِىْۤ اَبِىْۤ اَوْ يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ لِىْ ۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(80)\nFALAMMAA ASTAAYASOOA MINHO KHALASOOA NAJEEA QAALA KABEERUHUM ALAM TA’LAMOO ANNAL AABAAKUM QAD AAKHAZA A’LAYKUM MMAWSEQAN MENAL LAAHE WA MIN QABLO MAA FARRATTUM FEE YOOSUFA FALAN AABRAHA ARZA HATTAA YAAZANA LEE ABEE AW YAHKUMA LAAHO LEE WA HOWA KHAYRUR HAAKEMEEN.\nAnd when they despaired of (moving) him, they retired whispering (to each other); Said the eldest of them: “Know ye not how your father took from you a (firm) covenant in God’s name, (and) how failed ye about Joseph aforetime? So never will I leave this land until my father permitteth me or decideth God for me; And He is the Best of judges.\nاِرْجِعُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَبِيْكُمْ فَقُوْلُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَاۤ اِنَّ ابْنَكَ سَرَقَۚ وَمَا شَهِدْنَاۤ اِلَّا بِمَا عَلِمْنَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِلْغَيْبِ حٰفِظِيْنَ‏(81)\nAERJEU’OOA ELAA AABEEKUM FAQOOLOOA YAABAANAA INNAL ABNAKA SARAQA WA MAA SHAHIDNAA ILLAA BEMAA A’LIMNAA WA MAA KUNNAA LIL-GHAYBE HAAFEZEEN.\nReturn ye unto your father and say ye: “O’ our father! Verily thy son committed theft; we bear not witness but to what we have known and we could not guard against the unseen.\nوَسْئَلِ الْقَرْيَةَ الَّتِىْ كُنَّا فِيْهَا وَالْعِيْرَ الَّتِىْ اَقْبَلْنَا فِيْهَاؕ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(82)\nWASALE QARYATA LATEE KUNNAA FEEHAA WAL E’EERA LATEE AAQBALNAA FEEHAA WA INNAA LASAADEQOON.\nAnd inquire thou in the township in which we were and the caravan which we proceeded with; And verily we are truthful.\nقَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ اَنْفُسُكُمْ اَمْرًاؕ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيْلٌؕ عَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَنِىْ بِهِمْ جَمِيْعًاؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(83)\nQAALA BAL SAWLAT LAKUM ANFOSOKUM AAMRAN FASABRUN JAMEELUN A’ASAA LAAHO AN YYAATEENEAA BEHIM JAMEEA’AN INNAHU HOWA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nSaid he “Nay, your self have contrived the story (suitable) for you; so (my course) is comely patience; maybe God bringeth them unto me all together; Verily He is the All-Knowing, The All-Wise.\nوَتَوَلّٰى عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يٰۤاَسَفٰى عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ وَابْيَضَّتْ عَيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْحُزْنِ فَهُوَ كَظِيْمٌ‏(84)\nWA TAWALLAA A’NHUM WA QAALA YAASAFAA A’LAA YOOSUFA WAABYAZZAT A’AYNAAHU MENAL AL-HUZNE FAHOWA KAZEEMUN.\nAnd he turned away from them, and said: “Alas! my grief for Joseph!” and his eyes were whitened with the grief, and he was a represser (of grief).\nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ تَفْتَؤُا تَذْكُرُ يُوْسُفَ حَتّٰى تَكُوْنَ حَرَضًا اَوْ تَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْهَالِكِيْنَ‏(85)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE TAFTAUA TAZKURU YOOSUFA HATTAA TAKOONA HARAZAN AW TAKOONA MENAL AL-HAALEKEENA.\nSaid they: “By God! Thou wilt not cease to remember Joseph until thou art (seriously) ill or (until) thou art of the perished ones (dead).\nقَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اَشْكُوْا بَثِّىْ وَحُزْنِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَاَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(86)\nQAALA INNAMAA AASHKOOA BASSEAA WAHUZNEAA ELAL LAAHE WA A-A’LAMO MENAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nHe said: “I only complain of my distress and grief unto God, and I know from God what ye know not.\nيٰبَنِىَّ اذْهَبُوْا فَتَحَسَّسُوْا مِنْ يُّوْسُفَ وَاَخِيْهِ وَلَا تَايْئَسُوْا مِنْ رَّوْحِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يَايْئَسُ مِنْ رَّوْحِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(87)\nBANIYYA AZHABOOA FATAHASSASOOA MIN YYOOSUFA WA AKHEEHE WA LAA TAAYASOOA MIN RRAWHE LAAH INNAHU LAA YAAYASU MIN RRAWHE LAAHE ILLAA AL-QAWMU KAAFEROON.\nO’ my sons! go ye and inquire about Joseph and his Brother, and despair not of God’s mercy; Verily despaireth not of God’s mercy but the disbelieving people.\nفَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْعَزِيْزُ مَسَّنَا وَاَهْلَنَا الضُّرُّ وَجِئْنَا بِبِضَاعَةٍ مُّزْجٰٮةٍ فَاَوْفِ لَنَا الْكَيْلَ وَتَصَدَّقْ عَلَيْنَاؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَجْزِى الْمُتَصَدِّقِيْنَ‏(88)\nFALAMMAA DAKHALOO A’LAYHE QAALOO YAA AYYOHAL A’ZEEZUL MASSANAA WAAHLANAA AZ-ZURRU WAJENAA BEBEZAAA’ATIN MMUZJAATIN FAAWFE LANAA AL-KAYLA WATASADDAQ A’ALAYNAA INNAL LAAHA YAJZEAA AL-MUTASADDEQEENA.\nSo when they came in unto him said they: “O’ Aziz! distress hath touched us and our family; and we have (now) come (but) with scanty capital: so give us full measure and bestow thou charity on us; Verily God rewardeth the charitable ones.\nقَالَ هَلْ عَلِمْتُمْ مَّا فَعَلْتُمْ بِيُوْسُفَ وَاَخِيْهِ اِذْ اَنْتُمْ جٰهِلُوْنَ‏(89)\nQAALA HAL A’ALEMTUM MAA FAA’ALTUM BEEWSUFA WA AKHEEHE IZ ANTUM JAAHELOONA.\nSaid he: “Know ye what ye did unto Joseph and his brother when ye were ignorant (of the consequences).\nقَالُوْۤا ءَاِنَّكَ لَاَنْتَ يُوْسُفُؕ قَالَ اَنَا يُوْسُفُ وَهٰذَاۤ اَخِىْ قَدْ مَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَاؕ اِنَّهٗ مَنْ يَّتَّقِ وَيَصْبِرْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(90)\nQAALOO AANNAKA LAANTA YOOSUFU QAALA ANAA YOOSUFU WA AAKHEAA QAD MANNA LAAHO A’ALAYNAA INNAHU MAN YATTAQIL WAYASBER FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nThey said: “Art thou indeed Joseph?” Said he: “I am Joseph and this is my Brother; Indeed God hath been gracious unto us; Verily he who practiceth piety and is patient (is always rewarded) for verily God wasteth not the reward of the doers of good.\nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ لَقَدْ اٰثَرَكَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَا وَاِنْ كُنَّا لَخٰطِئِيْنَ‏(91)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE LAQAD AAASARAKA LAAHO A’LAYNAA WA KUNNAA LAKHAATEEENA.\nSaid they: “By God! indeed hath God chosen thee over us, and we were certainly guilty.\nقَالَ لَا تَثْرِيْبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْيَوْمَؕ يَغْفِرُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ وَهُوَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(92)\nQAALA LAA TASREEBA A’LAYKOMUL AL-YAWMA YAGHFERO LAAHO LAKUM WA HOWA AARHAMU AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nHe said: “(There shall be) no reproof against you (from) this day; God may forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of the merciful (ones).\nاِذْهَبُوْا بِقَمِيْصِىْ هٰذَا فَاَلْقُوْهُ عَلٰى وَجْهِ اَبِىْ يَاْتِ بَصِيْرًاۚ وَاْتُوْنِىْ بِاَهْلِكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(93)\nAEZHABOOA BEQAMEESEAA HAAZAA FAALQOOHU A’LAA WAJHIL ABEE TAKOONOO BASEERAA WAATOONEE BEAAHLEKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nTake ye this my shirt and cast it on the face of my father, he shall become seeing (recover his sight); and come ye unto me with all your family.\nوَلَمَّا فَصَلَتِ الْعِيْرُ قَالَ اَبُوْهُمْ اِنِّىْ لَاَجِدُ رِيْحَ يُوْسُفَ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ تُفَنِّدُوْنِ‏(94)\nWA LAMMAA FASALATE AL-E’EERU QAALA AABOOHUM INNEE LAAJEDU REEHA YOOSUFA LAWLAA AN TUFANNEDOONE.\nAnd when the caravan (with Yousuf’s shirt) had left (Egypt), their father (there in his place) said: “I feel the smell of Joseph, if ye think not that I dote.\nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ اِنَّكَ لَفِىْ ضَلٰلِكَ الْقَدِيْمِ‏(95)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE INNAKA LAFEE ZALAALEKA QADEEM.\nSaid they: “By God! Verily thou art in thy error.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَنْ جَآءَ الْبَشِيْرُ اَلْقٰٮهُ عَلٰى وَجْهِهٖ فَارْتَدَّ بَصِيْرًا  ؕۚ قَالَ اَلَمْ اَقُل لَّكُمْ ۚ ۙ اِنِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(96)\nFALAMMAA AN JAAA-A AL-BASHEERU AALQAAHU A’LAA WAJHEHI FAARTADDA BASEERAA QAALA ALAM AQUL LAKUM INNEE A-A’LAMO MENAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nSo when came the bearer of glad tidings, he cast it (the shirt) on his (Jacob’s) face, and (forthwith) returned (unto him) the eye-sight. He said: “Said I not unto you? Verily I know from God what ye know not.\nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا اسْتَغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا خٰطِئِيْنَ‏(97)\nQAALOO YAABAANAA ASTAGHFER LANAA ZUNOOBANAA INNAA KUNNAA KHAATE-EEN.\nSaid they: “O’ our father! Ask thou forgiveness for us, Verily we are guilty ones.\nقَالَ سَوْفَ اَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكُمْ رَبِّىْؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(98)\nQAALA SAWFA AASTAGHFERU LAKUM RABBEAA INNAHU HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nHe said: “Soon will I ask forgiveness for you from my Lord: Verily He is the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nفَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ اٰوٰٓى اِلَيْهِ اَبَوَيْهِ وَقَالَ ادْخُلُوْا مِصْرَ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ اٰمِنِيْنَؕ‏(99)\nFALAMMAA DAKHALOO A’LAA YOOSUFA AAAWAAA ELAYHE AABAWAYHE WA QAALA KHOLOO MESRA IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO AAAMENEENA.\nAnd when they entered the presence of Joseph, he accommodated his parents with himself, and said he: “Enter ye Egypt, if God willeth, (all) in security.\nوَرَفَعَ اَبَوَيْهِ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ وَخَرُّوْا لَهٗ سُجَّدًاۚ وَقَالَ يٰۤاَبَتِ هٰذَا تَاْوِيْلُ رُءْيَاىَ مِنْ قَبْلُقَدْ جَعَلَهَا رَبِّىْ حَقًّاؕ وَقَدْ اَحْسَنَ بِىْۤ اِذْ اَخْرَجَنِىْ مِنَ السِّجْنِ وَجَآءَ بِكُمْ مِّنَ الْبَدْوِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَنْ نَّزَغَ الشَّيْطٰنُ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَ اِخْوَتِىْؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ لَطِيْفٌ لِّمَا يَشَآءُؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(100)\nRA-FA-A’ AABAWAYHE A’LAL A’RSHIL WAKHARROOA LAHU SUJJADANW WA QAALA YAA HAAZAA TAAWEELU RUYAAAAA MIN QABLUQAD JAA’ALAHAA RABBEE HAQQAN WA QAD AHSANAL BEE IZ AAKHRAJANEAA MENAL AS-SEJNE WA JAAA-A BEKUM MENAL AL-BADWE MIN BA’DE AN NNAZAGHA SHAYTAANO BAYNEE WA BAYNA AEKHWATEAA INNAL RABBEE LATEEFUN LEMAA YASHAAU INNAHU HOWA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd raised he his parents to the throne, and they fell down unto him prostrating and said he “O’ my father! this is the interpretation of my dream of a foretime! Indeed my Lord hath made it come true; and indeed He was kind unto me when He took me out of the prison and hath brought you from the desert (into this town unto me) after hath sown Satan dissension between me and my brothers: Verily my Lord is Benignant unto whomsoever He willeth; Verily He is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nرَبِّ قَدْ اٰتَيْتَنِىْ مِنَ الْمُلْكِ وَ عَلَّمْتَنِىْ مِنْ تَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحَادِيْثِ ۚ فَاطِرَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اَنْتَ وَلِىّٖ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ تَوَفَّنِىْ مُسْلِمًا وَّاَلْحِقْنِىْ بِالصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(101)\nRABBE QAD AAATAYTANEAA MENAL AL-MULKE WA A’ALLAMTANEAA MIN TAAWEELE AL-AAHAADEESE FAATERA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE ANTA WALEAAA FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH TAWAFFANEAA MUSLEMAN WWAALHEQNEAA BE-SAALEHEEN.\nO’ My Lord! Indeed hast Thou given me of the dominion and taught me of the interpretation of events (dreams):(O’) Originator of the heavens and the earth! Thou (alone) art my guardian in this world and the hereafter; cause me die a Muslim (in submission unto Thee) and join me with the righteous.\nذٰلِكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوْحِيْهِ اِلَيْكَۚ وَمَا كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ اِذْ اَجْمَعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(102)\nZAALEKA MIN AANBAAE GHAYBE NOOHEEHE ELAYKA WA MAA KUNTA LADAYHIM IZ AAJMAU’OOA AAMRAHUM WA HUM YAMKOROON.\nThis is (one) of the tidings of the unseen (which) We reveal unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) and nor wast thou present with them (the brothers of Joseph) when they resolved their affair, and while they were devising their plans.\nوَمَاۤاَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتَ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(103)\nWAMAAAAKSARU NAASE WA LAW HARASTA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nAnd most people believe (it) not, though thou desirest it.\nوَمَا تَسْئَلُهُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(104)\nWA MAA TASALUHUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN HOWA ILLAA ZIKRUNW LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nWhat (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) Thou asketh not of them a recompense for it, for this, (it) is no other than an admonition unto (all) the worlds (of creation).\nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ اٰيَةٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ يَمُرُّوْنَ عَلَيْهَا وَهُمْ عَنْهَا مُعْرِضُوْنَ‏(105)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN AAYATIM FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE YAMURROONA A’LAYHAA WA HUM A’NHAA MUA’REZOONA.\nAnd how many a sign in the heavens and the earth which they pass by {day and night), (and) yet they turn away from them.\nوَمَا يُؤْمِنُ اَكْثَرُهُمْ بِاللّٰهِ اِلَّا وَهُمْ مُّشْرِكُوْنَ‏(106)\nWA MAA BIL LAAHE AKSAROHUM BIL-LAAHE ILLAA WA HUM MMUSHREKOONA.\nAnd believe not most of them, in God, except as polytheists.\nاَفَاَمِنُوْۤا اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمْ غَاشِيَةٌ مِّنْ عَذَابِ اللّٰهِ اَوْ تَاْتِيَهُمُ السَّاعَةُ بَغْتَةً وَّ هُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(107)\nAAFAAMENOOA AN TAATEEHUM GHAASHEETUN MIN A’ZAABIN LAAHE AW TAA-TEYAHOMUL SAA-A’TO BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nWhat! then feel they secure that there may come unto them an overwhelming chastisement from God or (that) cometh unto them the hour suddenly while they are unaware?\nقُلْ هٰذِهٖ سَبِيْلِىْۤ اَدْعُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ ؔعَلٰى بَصِيْرَةٍ اَنَا وَمَنِ اتَّبَعَنِىْؕ وَسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(108)\nQUL HAAZEHI SABEELEAA AADU’OOA ELAL LAAHE A’ALAA BASEERATIN ANAA MANIT ATTABAA’ANEAA SUBHAANAL LAAHE WA MAA ANAA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “This is my way, I invite (ye all) unto God; with clear sight, (which) I and he who followeth me (possesses); And glory be to God, and I am not of the polytheists.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ اِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ اَهْلِ الْقُرٰىؕ اَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ وَلَدَارُ الْاٰخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(109)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA ILLAA REJAALAN NNOOHEAA ELAYHIM MIN AHLIL AL-QURAA A-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WALADAARU AAKHERATE KHAYRUL LIL-LAZEENA TAQAW AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd We sent not (apostles) before thee but men unto whom We revealed, from (among) the people of the towns; What! travel they not in the land that they might see what hath been the end of those before them? And certainly the abode of the hereafter is the best for those who guard them selves (against evil); What! Do ye not then understand?\nحَتّٰۤى اِذَا اسْتَيْئَسَ الرُّسُلُ وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ قَدْ كُذِبُوْا جَآءَهُمْ نَصْرُنَا ۙ فَنُجِّىَ مَنْ نَّشَآءُ ؕ وَلَا يُرَدُّ بَاْسُنَا عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(110)\nHATTAA EZAA ASTAYASA ROSOLO WA ZANNOO ANNAHUM QAD KUZEBOOA JAAA-AHUM NASRUNAA FANUJJEAAA MAN NNASHAAU WA LAA YORADDO BAASUNAA A’NIL QAWMIL MUJREMEEN.\nTill, when the apostles despaired and deemed they were indeed belied, came unto them Our help; and delivered We whomsoever We willed; and Our wrath is not warded off from the people (who are) guilty.\nلَقَدْ كَانَ فِىْ قَصَصِهِمْ عِبْرَةٌ لِّاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِؕ مَا كَانَ حَدِيْثًا يُّفْتَرٰى وَلٰكِنْ تَصْدِيْقَ الَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَتَفْصِيْلَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(111)\nLAQAD KAANA FEE QASASEHEM E’EBRATUN LEAOOLEAA AL-AALBAABE MAA KAANA HADEESAN YYUFTARAA WA LAAKIL TASDEEQA LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WATAFSEELA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAHUDAN WA RAHMATAL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nIndeed (there) in the histories of theirs, is a lesson for men of understanding; it is not a tale which hath been forged, but a confirmation of what went before it, A detailed exposition of all things and a guide and a mercy unto people who believe.",
  "merits": "Surah Yusuf has 111 ayaat and was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that whoever recites this Surah and teaches his family members how to recite it also, Allah (s.w.t.) will make the final moments before his death (sakaraatul mawt) easy for him to bear and will remove jealousy from his heart.\nIt has been narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq that whoever recited this Surah daily, he will be raised on the day of Qiyamah with the handsomeness of Prophet Yusuf (a.s.) and he will be protected from the fear and discomfort of this day. He will be raised among the pious servants of Allah (s.w.t.). This Surah also keeps one’s heart safe from illegitimate lustful desires.\nThe sixth Imam (a.s.) has also said that if a person drinks the water in which this Surah has been dissolved, then his sustenance will be easier to reach and he will be made from the people of Jannah."
}
